//? Title: HITS: alternating endorsements, actual histories and degenerate graphs
//? Subtitle: A closed-form four-vertex reference and bounded native traces
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
A hub endorses authorities, and an authority receives endorsements from hubs.
HITS turns that circular description into alternating matrix products. We
calculate a single-edge example, retain the original four-vertex graph and
derive its golden-ratio scores, then inspect the actual update history. Edgeless
graphs, repeated edges and disconnected ties expose the limits of an
unconditional principal-eigenvector interpretation. Native counters distinguish
selected producing work from timing and capture overhead.
)

\toc

> One edge, two different roles

For the directed edge 0 to 1, both initial vectors are (q,q), with q=1/sqrt(2).
The first raw authority vector is (0,q), so normalization gives (0,1). Using
these new authorities, the raw and normalized hub vectors are (1,0). The largest
change is q; the second paired update changes nothing. The following values and
diagram come from those actual producing steps.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/hits_tiny.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    const auto t = dm::algorithms::hits_trace(2, {{0, 1}});
    std::print("| paired update | authority norm | hub norm | joint change |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
    for (const auto &v : t.steps)
        std::print("| {} | {:.9f} | {:.9f} | {:.9f} |\n", v.iteration,
                   v.authority_norm, v.hub_norm, v.change);
    const auto &v = t.steps.front();
    dm::graphics::Diagram d(65, 1100);
    dm::graphics::DiagramNodeStyle style;
    style.width = 4.7;
    style.height = 2.8;
    style.font_size = 21;
    d.node("old", {0, 0},
           std::format("Previous hubs\n({:.3f}, {:.3f})", t.initial_hubs[0],
                       t.initial_hubs[1]), style).node("a", {7, 0},
                                                       std::format(
                                                       "New authorities\n({:.3f}, {:.3f})",
                                                       v.authorities[0],
                                                       v.authorities[1]), style).node("h", {14, 0}, std::format("New hubs\n({:.3f}, {:.3f})", v.hubs[0], v.hubs[1]), style).edge("old", "a", "A transpose + norm").edge("a", "h", "A + norm").text({7, 3}, "Supplied graph: 0 points to 1", 25).save_svg("build/hits_tiny.svg");
    if (t.steps.size() != 2 || t.run.result.hubs[0] != 1 ||
        t.run.result.authorities[1] != 1)
        throw std::runtime_error("single edge");
}
```
