> Producing work and the cost of retaining history

For n vertices, m supplied edge entries and K completed paired updates, the
kernel visits Km authority edges and Km hub edges, 2Kn squared norm values and
Kn change-test vertices. It divides n values for each nonzero norm. These
counters omit validation, initialization, zero-filling, score copying,
allocation and trace storage; they are not FLOPs or elapsed time. Including
initialization, ordinary execution costs O(n+K(n+m)) time and O(n)
working/output storage beyond the borrowed edge list.

The outgoing-star family below supplies edges 0 to every other vertex. It
converges after two paired updates at the chosen tolerance. Each row comes from
its actual execution; the measured counters illustrate the per-pass bound rather
than a universal iteration count.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/hits_work.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    std::vector<double> x, edges, norms, changes;
    std::print("| n | m | actual K | authority edges | hub edges | norm values | divisions | change vertices |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
    for (std::size_t n : {4, 16, 64, 256, 1024}) {
        std::vector<dm::algorithms::HitsEdge> e;
        for (std::size_t v = 1; v < n; ++v) e.emplace_back(0, v);
        const auto r = dm::algorithms::hits_run(n, e);
        const auto &w = r.work;
        x.push_back(n);
        edges.push_back(w.authority_edges + w.hub_edges);
        norms.push_back(w.norm_values);
        changes.push_back(w.change_vertices);
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n", n, e.size(),
                   r.result.iterations, w.authority_edges, w.hub_edges,
                   w.norm_values, w.divisions, w.change_vertices);
        if (w.authority_edges != e.size() * r.result.iterations ||
            w.norm_values != 2 * n * r.result.iterations)
            throw std::runtime_error("work counters");
    }
    auto p = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
    p.line(x, edges, "edge additions", {37, 99, 235}, 2.).line(x, norms,
                                                               "norm terms",
                                                               {220, 38, 38}, 2.).line(x, changes, "change vertices", {22, 163, 74}, 2.).title("Outgoing stars: selected actual producing visits").x_label("vertices n").y_label("selected loop visits").y_limits(0, 5500).save_svg("build/hits_work.svg");
}
```
