\caption(Selected producing visits grow with graph size for this two-update family; allocation and retained-history costs are outside these counts. The edge-addition and norm-term curves nearly overlap because their exact counts are 4(n-1) and 4n.)
\alttext(Three curves show actual edge additions, squared norm terms and change-test vertex visits as star size increases.)

Tracing retains 2n initial score values and then one record plus 4n
raw/normalized score values per complete iteration. Its logical capture count is
2n+K(1+4n), not bytes or peak RAM. The initial count is admitted before score
allocation; each whole record is admitted online before its iteration work.
Limits throw rather than truncate or replay. Default vertex, edge-entry and
capture caps are each one million; zero disables each policy. The capture cap is
ignored by nontracing hits_run. Histories own their vectors and add O(Kn)
storage. Legacy hits has no optional policy caps but retains checked counts and
container limits.

> Controls: zeros, initialization, duplicate weighting and ties

An edgeless graph maps both vectors to zero. With n=4 the first change is 1/2
and the next is zero, so the default call takes two updates. Empty n=0 with a
positive budget takes one empty update; zero budget takes none. Returning zero
scores is the deliberate zero-norm branch, not a unit dominant eigenvector.

Disconnected equal-strength components can share the dominant eigenvalue. For
edges 0 to 2 and 1 to 3, uniform initialization preserves equal hub scores at 0
and 1. Duplicating 0 to 2 in the original graph instead increases its
endorsement multiplicity and changes the solution. Self-links are accepted as
well. These conventions must match the graph one intends to analyze.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/hits_controls.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    using E = dm::algorithms::HitsEdge;
    const std::vector<std::vector<E>> cases = {{}, {}, {{0, 2}, {0, 3}, {1, 2}},
                                               {{0, 2}, {0, 2}, {0, 3}, {1, 2}},
                                               {{0, 2}, {1, 3}}};
    std::vector<double> x, h0, h1;
    std::print("| case | budget | iterations | has step | hub 0 | hub 1 |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | --- | ---: | ---: |\n");
    const std::vector<std::string> labels = {"edgeless", "initial only",
                                             "original", "duplicate edge",
                                             "tied components"};
    for (std::size_t i = 0; i < cases.size(); ++i) {
        const std::size_t budget = i == 1 ? 0 : 1000;
        const auto r = dm::algorithms::hits_run(4, cases[i], 1e-12, budget);
        x.push_back(i + 1);
        h0.push_back(r.result.hubs[0]);
        h1.push_back(r.result.hubs[1]);
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {:.9f} | {:.9f} |\n", labels[i],
                   budget, r.result.iterations, r.has_step, r.result.hubs[0],
                   r.result.hubs[1]);
    }
    const auto exact =
        dm::algorithms::hits_trace(2, {{0, 1}}, 1e-12, 1, {2, 1, 13});
    bool rejected = false;
    try {
        (void) dm::algorithms::hits_trace(2, {{0, 1}}, 1e-12, 1, {2, 1, 12});
    } catch (const std::length_error &) { rejected = true; }
    std::print("\nOne-step capture units {}; one-short policy rejected {}; empty graph iterations {}; self-loop score {}.\n",
               exact.captured_entries, rejected,
               dm::algorithms::hits(0, {}).iterations,
               dm::algorithms::hits(1, {{0, 0}}).hubs[0]);
    auto p = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
    p.points(x, h0, "hub 0", {37, 99, 235}, 7.).points(x, h1, "hub 1",
                                                       {220, 38, 38}, 5.).title(
        "Controls: case numbers follow the table").x_label("case number").y_label("actual returned hub score").y_limits(-.05, 1.3).save_svg("build/hits_controls.svg");
    if (!rejected || exact.captured_entries != 13)
        throw std::runtime_error("capture policy");
}
```
